# GuildCloud console — environment.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. These are the ONLY variables
# the Next.js app reads; everything else the platform needs lives either in
# Supabase Vault (Proxmox tokens, Tailscale OAuth, Resend key) or in the site
# worker's own /etc/guildcloud/worker.env — see deploy/site-worker/env.example.
#
# Full from-zero setup, including where each value comes from:
# docs/REPLICATION.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — required. The console cannot start without these.
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The publishable ("anon") key. Safe in the browser: it is a public identifier,
# and RLS is what actually constrains access. Never put the service_role key
# here — a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is compiled into client bundles.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site URL — optional locally, required in any real deployment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute origin of this deployment, no trailing slash. Used to build the
# links that go into invite emails and device-enrollment scripts, so a wrong
# value produces mails and enrollment commands pointing at the wrong host.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3100 when unset (see lib/site-url.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT used by the console. Listed so nobody adds them here by mistake.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  Edge Functions only (set with `supabase secrets
#                              set`, and injected automatically for functions
#                              deployed to the hosted project). It bypasses RLS
#                              entirely; it must never reach the Next.js app or
#                              a browser.
#   SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET        Only scripts/mint-worker-token.mjs, run by an
#                              operator on demand. Not a deployment variable.
#   SUPABASE_WORKER_TOKEN      The site worker's own credential, set in
#                              /etc/guildcloud/worker.env on the worker LXC.
#   RESEND_API_KEY             Stored in Supabase Vault as `resend_api_key` and
#                              read by the send-invite-email Edge Function.
